{
  "_notes": [
    "AC/DC (v1.70, 2012, Stern).",
    "Stern SAM platform. ARM AT91 CPU, NVRAM at CPU 0x02100000.",
    "Scores are 4-byte little-endian integers.",
    "Stride between entries is 0x24 bytes.",
    "Verified against NVRAM data with real scores.",
    "The champion record starts at the name, not the score: 24 bytes of name and 0xFF fill, the",
    "score at +24, then a 16-bit checksum (0xFFFF minus the sum of the preceding bytes) and two",
    "slack bytes. That framing is what the checksum proves -- it validates on all five records when",
    "they are taken to start at the name and on none when taken to start at the score -- and it",
    "fixes a pairing error: each name was previously read from the following record, so the Grand",
    "Champion's score was reported against the first-place player's initials. With the records",
    "framed correctly this game's factory defaults read JDB/75,000,000, LFS/55,000,000 and so on,",
    "the same set the rest of the SAM family ships (SSR/75,000,000 here).",
    "bytes have read zero in every image captured, so the width is taken from the record's",
    "The record is 36 bytes with the checksum at +32, so four bytes sit between the 4-byte score at",
    "+24 and the checksum. They read zero in every image captured (163 records across five games)",
    "and their purpose is not established: they are consistent with the upper half of a 64-bit score,",
    "but this game's champion-threshold table at 0x021024F8 stores its thresholds as 4-byte values",
    "with a complement check byte, which is what a 32-bit score would be compared against. The score",
    "is therefore declared as 4 bytes until a value above 2^32 is observed or the ROM is disassembled."
  ],
